==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=derby (disambiguation)|derby}}

===Etymology===
From [[w:Epsom Derby|Epsom Derby]] horse race, named after [[w:Edward Smith-Stanley, 12th Earl of Derby|Edward Smith-Stanley, 12th Earl of Derby]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdɑː(ɹ).bi/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(ɹ)bi|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈdɝ.bi/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)bi|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Derby (horse race)}}
{{en-noun|derbies}}

# Any of several [[annual]] [[horse race]]s.
# By extension, any organized [[race]].
# {{label|en|US}} A [[bowler hat]]
#* '''1906''', O. Henry, ''[[s:The Green Door|The Green Door]]''
#*: He began to fan her with his hat. That was successful, for he struck her nose with the brim of his '''derby''' and she opened her eyes.
# {{label|en|sports}} A [[local derby]].
